                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_53\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (\"bugfix: retargeting logic error\") modifies Util.retargetAnimation/retargetTrack in\nsrc/main/java/maud/Util.java. Before the fix, the code was:\n\n    sourceTrack = MyAnimation.findTrack(sourceAnimation, iSource);\n    if (sourceTrack != null) { // handle null sourceTrack\n        BoneTrack track;\n        track = retargetTrack(sourceAnimation, sourceTrack,\n                sourceSkeleton, targetSkeleton, mapping, iTarget);\n        result.addTrack(track);\n    }\n\nThe fix removes this null-guard entirely and instead always calls retargetTrack, pushing the\nnull-handling into retargetTrack itself (which now synthesizes a single bind-pose keyframe when\nsourceTrack is null, instead of silently omitting the target bone's track altogether). The bug was\nthat any target bone mapped to a source bone with no corresponding animation track was completely\nskipped when building the retargeted animation, rather than being given a bind-pose track \u2014 a\nlogic error in the retargeting process.\n\nTracing the history of this code in the candidates:\n\n- candidate_36 contains an earlier version of retargetAnimation/retargetTrack where sourceTrack is\n  looked up *inside* retargetTrack via sourceBoneIndex, with no null check at all (this would NPE on\n  a missing track \u2014 a different bug, not the one described in the fix).\n\n- candidate_53 refactors retargetTrack to take the already-resolved BoneTrack sourceTrack as a\n  parameter, and at the call site introduces:\n      sourceTrack = MyAnimation.findTrack(sourceAnimation, iSource);\n      if (sourceTrack != null) {\n          ...\n          result.addTrack(track);\n      }\n  This is exactly the problematic \"skip the track when null\" logic that the fix later removes.\n  Inside retargetTrack, candidate_53 also adds `Validate.nonNull(sourceTrack, \"source track\")`,\n  reinforcing that null sourceTrack was being treated as an error/skip condition rather than a\n  legitimate bind-pose case.\n\n- candidate_54 only adds the comment \"// handle null sourceTrack\" to the same `if` line \u2014 no\n  behavioral change.\n\n- candidate_55 is identical to the fix commit diff itself (the actual bug fix), removing the\n  null-check/skip behavior.\n\nSince candidate_53 is the first commit to introduce the `if (sourceTrack != null) { ... }` skip\nlogic that the fix directly reverses, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
